It is Friday lunch time.
I go to the bakery Prakash mentioned.
There is a good crowd in the shop.
There are many sweets in the glass cabinet there.
I think that Deepa will like this.
I see halwas of many colours.
There is halwa in red, black, and yellow colours there.
I shall buy a mixed halwa box.
"Brother, I want a mixed halwa box," I tell the shopkeeper.
"Certainly, how many kilos do you want?" he asks.
"Half a kilo is enough," I reply.
He puts halwas of many colours into a box.
"This is two hundred rupees," he says.
I give him the money.
I will take this when I go to Deepa's house tonight.
I am sure that this is a good gift.
